WEBVTT

00:09.980 --> 00:14.110
Dear Mother and Father, 
who are in heaven...

00:15.610 --> 00:17.540
Can't wait to fight...

00:21.630 --> 00:25.120
I might just die today.

00:27.580 --> 00:31.130
I want the first crack 
at the Crystal Helmet!

00:31.130 --> 00:34.260
No, you ornery pup, I'll go first!

00:35.250 --> 00:37.640
I'm tired of waiting!

00:37.640 --> 00:43.650
Who... Who... Who in the 
world are these people?!

01:01.960 --> 01:09.550
The Warrior Princess and the Barbaric King

02:25.500 --> 02:27.710
Preparations for a meeting, you said?

02:27.710 --> 02:31.160
Right. I've gathered the 
elders of the various tribes

02:31.160 --> 02:34.350
so that I can introduce you to them.

02:34.350 --> 02:35.210
As for the venue...

02:35.830 --> 02:38.220
Over there. Do you see it?

02:38.810 --> 02:41.210
The original home of our people,

02:41.210 --> 02:43.720
the grand village overseen
by the Great Chief.

02:44.460 --> 02:46.520
Lakeside Village.

02:47.070 --> 02:50.730
The largest settlement in these parts.

02:51.490 --> 02:53.660
I had noticed it in the distance, but...

02:53.660 --> 02:57.890
Wait, why are you telling me 
such crucial information?!

02:57.890 --> 02:59.740
Isn't it some sort of military secret?!

03:02.500 --> 03:04.650
What are you worried about?

03:05.180 --> 03:06.990
Theoretically speaking...

03:08.150 --> 03:11.710
If I were to escape 
and be rescued by my forces,

03:11.710 --> 03:15.250
having knowledge of your 
settlements and territory...

03:15.250 --> 03:19.910
Couldn't that potentially 
lead to your destruction?

03:25.610 --> 03:27.820
I am asking a serious question!

03:27.820 --> 03:32.920
Or is it that you simply think 
I have no chance of escaping?!

03:33.460 --> 03:35.690
It's not that I'm underestimating you.

03:38.050 --> 03:44.030
But, Sera, weren't you 
enchanted by my shaven face?

03:49.290 --> 03:51.500
I was just confused!

03:58.870 --> 04:01.630
Do you need to keep dragging 
that back up? It's so childish!

04:01.630 --> 04:03.350
Embarrassed, aren't you?

04:03.350 --> 04:04.770
That's so charming.

04:04.770 --> 04:05.660
Charm...?!

04:07.140 --> 04:09.940
Besides, your worries will be moot

04:09.940 --> 04:12.020
if you lose the desire 
to return to your home.

04:13.520 --> 04:16.720
I've stated that my intent 
is to make you my wife.

04:16.720 --> 04:18.900
Which includes making 
sure you fall for me.

04:20.650 --> 04:23.610
Seriously, where does all 
this confidence come from?!

04:25.530 --> 04:27.670
They already sound like a couple...

04:35.670 --> 04:40.420
Who... Who... Who in the 
world are these people?!

04:40.700 --> 04:44.800
Master Thunder Voice! 
I ask your leave to battle this woman!

04:44.800 --> 04:47.300
My axe can't wait much longer!

04:47.300 --> 04:49.810
Just once! I've got to fight her!

04:50.250 --> 04:52.150
So, it's revenge.

04:52.540 --> 04:56.310
For all of their fellow 
barbarians I've slain...

04:57.310 --> 05:00.700
No need to be so tense, Sera.

05:00.700 --> 05:02.820
I'll explain things to them.

05:06.310 --> 05:08.530
My brave warriors!

05:08.530 --> 05:11.330
I thank you for welcoming 
the Crystal Helmet!

05:13.080 --> 05:18.340
But she is here today to 
break bread with the elders!

05:18.340 --> 05:22.370
And while I understand your feelings when 
faced with such a powerful opponent,

05:22.370 --> 05:23.950
I ask that you calm yourselves!

05:27.540 --> 05:31.850
Well, if that's what Master
Thundering Voice says, so be it!

05:31.850 --> 05:32.850
Wha—?!

05:32.850 --> 05:35.860
A-All that bloodlust... gone.

05:32.850 --> 05:35.160
Guess we got ahead of ourselves!

05:38.350 --> 05:41.380
A powerful opponent... did he mean me?

05:42.020 --> 05:44.180
What's going on here? What is this?

05:44.530 --> 05:46.730
Why have they all gathered here?

05:47.890 --> 05:51.870
To welcome you, along with waiting 
for a chance to spar with you.

05:51.870 --> 05:55.030
They're waiting for a chance... to spar?

05:57.380 --> 06:02.750
Hang on, none of this makes any sense! 
Shouldn't they be out for revenge?

06:03.210 --> 06:07.630
Revenge? Were you really 
worried about that?

06:09.670 --> 06:14.470
My brave warriors. Do any of you have 
a vendetta against the Crystal Helmet?!

06:16.090 --> 06:19.270
If not, then make way!

06:23.230 --> 06:28.150
We warriors bear no ill will!

06:33.540 --> 06:34.160
Come along.

06:36.090 --> 06:39.750
Surely they're just obeying the 
orders of the Great Chief's son?

06:40.370 --> 06:41.900
Well, so be it!

06:46.980 --> 06:49.490
I am a knight commander 
of the Eastern Expedition.

06:49.900 --> 06:52.930
I cannot lose my composure, 
regardless of the situation!

06:58.150 --> 07:00.050
Crystal Helmet!

07:02.310 --> 07:08.190
Your martial display from the 
other day... was truly brilliant!

07:08.190 --> 07:09.240
Huh?

07:09.880 --> 07:11.410
He's right!

07:11.410 --> 07:14.330
To trade blows with Master Thundering 
Voice... You're a hell of a warrior!

07:14.330 --> 07:16.200
And a beauty, to boot!

07:16.440 --> 07:18.620
I wish she could've been my wife!

07:18.620 --> 07:22.240
I still remember those 
blows that shattered stone.

07:22.240 --> 07:26.490
A damn fine woman. Here's hoping she 
bears some good, strong children!

07:26.960 --> 07:31.470
Wh-What are you saying?!
Don't you realize I'm an enemy commander?!

07:31.470 --> 07:34.770
It's as I said. They bear you no grudge.

07:36.310 --> 07:39.850
We have an appreciation 
for those who are strong.

07:40.100 --> 07:45.970
Those are the values of my people, 
and in particular, these men.

08:30.590 --> 08:31.610
Cersei.

08:32.150 --> 08:33.780
What is it, sir?

08:34.030 --> 08:36.510
That house happens to be boiling water.

08:36.940 --> 08:39.280
You and Sera will enjoy their hospitality.

08:40.660 --> 08:45.170
What will you be doing in 
the meantime, Master Veor?

08:45.400 --> 08:48.410
Just a few errands.

08:48.410 --> 08:51.870
I'll have an initial discussion 
with the elders, as well.

08:51.870 --> 08:52.920
It won't be long.

08:53.550 --> 08:57.250
You there! People of this home!
I am the Thundering Voice.

08:58.120 --> 08:59.500
Master Thundering Voice?

09:03.430 --> 09:05.380
How may I help you?

09:06.830 --> 09:08.870
Sorry to suddenly call on you,

09:08.870 --> 09:11.460
but I ask that you share your 
hot water with these two.

09:11.460 --> 09:14.510
The blond one is going to be my wife.

09:14.510 --> 09:15.250
Wha—?!

09:15.250 --> 09:17.660
Oh, well that's wonderful news!

09:18.040 --> 09:21.120
My, my, my, and she's quite the beauty!

09:21.120 --> 09:24.950
And she has the same color eyes 
as the Great Chief's wife!

09:30.680 --> 09:35.000
Well, it seems to me Master Thundering 
Voice is bound to be satisfied!

09:35.550 --> 09:38.550
Come right on in, don't be shy!

09:36.820 --> 09:41.070
W-Wait! We just met! You're being 
too familiar! Listen to me...!

09:39.590 --> 09:41.070
Look after her.

09:47.980 --> 09:50.970
I didn't mean any harm. 
Hope you can forgive me.

09:52.190 --> 09:53.310
It's fine.

09:53.310 --> 09:55.770
Forgiveness is a knight's virtue.

09:56.180 --> 09:58.950
It's nice that Master Thundering 
Voice has such a kind wife.

09:59.360 --> 10:01.190
Don't call me that!

10:01.190 --> 10:02.200
Oh, dear.

10:04.590 --> 10:07.510
Y'know, we should put 
some medicinal tea on.

10:07.510 --> 10:08.500
Could you grab it?

10:18.710 --> 10:21.600
Good boy, Gatar, remembering where it was.

10:22.430 --> 10:24.600
You put medicinal herbs in your tea...?

10:24.600 --> 10:28.790
Sure do. It's pretty common 
around these parts.

10:28.790 --> 10:30.880
I hope you like it.

10:30.880 --> 10:34.110
But with these numbers, 
we'll need more hot water.

10:36.200 --> 10:37.930
Go turn the fire up.

10:40.630 --> 10:41.490
What are they doing?

10:41.820 --> 10:43.990
Off to grab some more firewood.

10:43.990 --> 10:47.990
They seem awfully 
sure-footed for their age.

10:47.990 --> 10:50.370
Solid foundations for a warrior, 
in ones so young....

10:58.940 --> 11:01.660
They're mostly just mimicking us.

11:02.040 --> 11:05.780
Ena's been a good example
for Gatar, lately, too.

11:05.780 --> 11:07.460
It's been a big relief.

11:07.460 --> 11:09.580
It works both ways.

11:11.100 --> 11:14.900
So these two... aren't actually related?

11:17.090 --> 11:19.150
Should be ready, now.

11:19.150 --> 11:21.990
Here you are. 
Drink up before it cools, now.

11:27.690 --> 11:28.680
It's good!

11:31.650 --> 11:37.300
Even a noble like yourself can appreciate 
the rustic flavor of this tea?

11:37.300 --> 11:39.820
It's got a very distinct aroma,

11:39.820 --> 11:42.290
but it's refreshing in a way 
that more than justifies it.

11:42.290 --> 11:46.050
Almost as if the medicinal herbs are 
soaking throughout my entire body.

11:46.290 --> 11:51.330
Well, the herbs are high quality, and 
come from the spirits of the Sacred Tree.

11:52.440 --> 11:55.280
I'm real glad you like it.

11:55.280 --> 11:57.030
Care for more?

11:57.370 --> 11:58.320
Yes, please!

12:10.140 --> 12:13.640
Are communal houses like this 
common in barbarian territory?

12:14.890 --> 12:17.370
You two don't seem to be related.

12:17.370 --> 12:20.460
And I can't imagine it's just 
the four of you living here.

12:21.110 --> 12:23.590
Are your husbands some of the 
warriors that were outside?

12:24.270 --> 12:25.950
Well...

12:27.150 --> 12:31.100
the truth is our husbands 
passed away a while ago.

12:32.850 --> 12:37.220
Mine died in the war, to the west, 
while this one was still in my belly.

12:37.220 --> 12:41.360
Got wounded in a bad way... 
and that was that.

12:46.760 --> 12:50.990
Then they were victims of the 
Eastern Expedition... of my army.

12:52.140 --> 12:54.830
It was necessary to secure
resources that our people need.

12:55.310 --> 12:58.090
And a fight between soldiers 
on opposing sides.

12:58.600 --> 13:01.790
There's no need for me to feel 
sympathy for these barbarians.

13:03.990 --> 13:07.640
If... only I could bring 
myself to believe that.

13:15.930 --> 13:20.910
I cannot offer apologies for the 
lives lost in our army's expedition.

13:22.020 --> 13:23.100
But I accept your hate.

13:24.010 --> 13:26.860
I was defeated, and taken captive.

13:27.250 --> 13:29.910
You two have the right 
to avenge your husbands.

13:32.280 --> 13:33.450
Say what?

13:35.860 --> 13:40.040
Revenge... why would we want that?

13:41.370 --> 13:45.740
You have to ask? 
The one who took their lives...

13:47.330 --> 13:49.510
It might have been me!

13:54.420 --> 13:58.680
I'm a bit sad that my boy doesn't 
remember his father's face,

14:04.530 --> 14:08.330
but he was lucky enough to be 
aside his father after he passed.

14:12.550 --> 14:15.350
And I was lucky enough 
to be left with him.

14:16.530 --> 14:18.290
It ain't just war, either.

14:18.610 --> 14:22.460
The men, whether it's dragon 
hunting, beast hunting,

14:22.460 --> 14:24.550
sometimes even monster hunting...

14:25.050 --> 14:27.850
Either they get their limbs hurt 
so bad they can't fight anymore,

14:27.850 --> 14:30.300
or age and weaken until they get eaten...

14:35.060 --> 14:39.060
One way or another, 
they're gonna end up dying in a fight.

14:39.410 --> 14:43.650
So I really don't know what to do 
when you look so torn up about it.

14:44.910 --> 14:48.320
The warriors from before, 
and now these women...

14:49.260 --> 14:51.730
Do the barbarians really 
view life and death

14:51.730 --> 14:55.330
so differently than we do in Illdoren?

15:07.820 --> 15:08.550
What's that sound?

15:09.230 --> 15:09.970
A dragon whistle...

15:10.320 --> 15:11.560
We're under attack!

15:42.830 --> 15:45.130
Wh-What is this thing?

15:45.130 --> 15:47.880
I-It's a type of dragon 
called a Tsukebikeshi.

15:48.250 --> 15:49.650
When you make a fire in the woods,

15:49.650 --> 15:51.720
it tends to seek out the 
source of the smoke...

15:51.720 --> 15:54.510
And that same habit led it to us.

15:55.310 --> 15:59.700
But it's strange. The Tsukebikeshi 
around here don't approach villages.

15:59.700 --> 16:02.520
They've learned how they'll 
be attacked if they do.

16:02.910 --> 16:04.980
Speculate later. For now, run!

16:04.980 --> 16:06.650
S-Sure thing.

16:11.900 --> 16:12.710
Not good!

16:12.710 --> 16:14.160
We've got its attention, now.

16:17.190 --> 16:18.980
W-We need to run!

16:18.980 --> 16:21.500
If something were to happen to you, 
I couldn't face my master!

16:21.500 --> 16:22.520
I refuse.

16:23.420 --> 16:25.800
Of all the idiotic—
are you trying to die?!

16:25.800 --> 16:27.630
I'd ask you the same, fool!

16:28.910 --> 16:33.840
You barbarians are too used 
to the deaths of others.

16:33.840 --> 16:35.290
It gets on my nerves.

16:35.930 --> 16:40.110
Besides, odd eyes... 
actually, let me use your name...

16:40.110 --> 16:44.100
Cersei. Who do you think 
you're dealing with?

16:45.050 --> 16:48.810
I am a knight commander of 
the the kingdom of Illdoren—

16:51.140 --> 16:53.670
Serafina de Lavillant!

16:58.680 --> 17:01.610
W-With the fire tongs? That's crazy!

17:01.610 --> 17:03.540
You shouldn't be fighting a 
dragon with that kind of—

17:03.540 --> 17:05.210
Stop talking. You're a distraction.

17:13.570 --> 17:17.560
Besides, the first blow 
made it clear enough.

17:17.990 --> 17:23.310
This mockery of a bird is nothing 
compared to that bearded oaf's sword!

17:23.730 --> 17:27.280
And more than that, as a 
knight, if there are those

17:27.280 --> 17:29.940
behind me, whom I must defend, 
then I will never retreat!

17:41.260 --> 17:44.040
Don't just stand there?! Run, already!

17:44.040 --> 17:45.630
R-Right!

17:45.630 --> 17:47.100
B-But...

17:47.560 --> 17:52.090
I can deal with an enemy like this in the
 time it takes you all to get to safety!

17:55.640 --> 17:57.720
And more than that, you're in the way!

17:59.240 --> 18:01.970
I-I'm going to mock you if you die!

18:03.980 --> 18:05.820
Pay attention, bird.

18:07.700 --> 18:09.600
You get to deal with me!

18:31.540 --> 18:32.600
Master Thundering Voice!

18:32.600 --> 18:34.420
How many of them entered the village?

18:34.420 --> 18:35.620
Four of them.

18:35.620 --> 18:39.600
See if there's anyone who 
was unable to get away.

18:39.600 --> 18:41.840
Your first priority is 
the villagers' safety!

18:41.840 --> 18:42.890
Y-Yes, sir!

18:43.380 --> 18:48.920
Sera was with Cersei. 
She likely got away safely, then.

18:50.460 --> 18:51.980
Let's put an end to these pests!

19:05.150 --> 19:07.260
Where is the last one?!

19:07.670 --> 19:09.160
Master Veor!

19:10.060 --> 19:11.170
Cersei?

19:11.570 --> 19:15.420
A... A Tsukebikeshi landed 
on the house from earlier!

19:16.430 --> 19:19.670
Miss Sera fought so we could get—

19:23.270 --> 19:24.600
So fast.

19:31.080 --> 19:36.190
I thought I'd have more options out in 
the open, but it's faster than I am!

19:49.560 --> 19:53.030
Not only that, but given 
its focus on me...

19:53.030 --> 19:55.460
I have plenty of stamina left, but—

20:09.160 --> 20:12.630
Charging at me the second 
I'm disarmed, eh?

20:12.630 --> 20:14.410
A clever creature.

20:18.680 --> 20:21.030
After invading their lands...

20:22.450 --> 20:26.440
Showing mercy for the weak may 
be little more than hypocrisy.

20:30.440 --> 20:34.200
But now I will have lived, 
and died, as a knight.

20:36.620 --> 20:38.290
Sera!

20:38.290 --> 20:39.800
Cover your ears!

20:58.140 --> 21:00.510
Forgive me, Sera. I was running late.

21:06.140 --> 21:07.490
As the next Great Chief,

21:07.490 --> 21:11.150
there are no thanks I can 
offer you that are sufficient

21:11.580 --> 21:14.710
to convey my gratitude for protecting 
Cersei and the people of this village.

21:17.430 --> 21:21.460
But more than anything... 
I am truly relieved...

21:23.330 --> 21:24.720
that you're all right.

21:32.230 --> 21:35.480
Huh? Why... What is this?

21:35.480 --> 21:37.930
Why am I crying?

21:39.730 --> 21:40.650
Why?

22:01.980 --> 22:03.970
Master Veor!

22:10.850 --> 22:13.600
Translation: Lee Francis

Timing: Andy Ellis

Editing: Zachary Carlysle

Quality Control: Salem Alabanza

Translation Check: Sho Stifler
